    "result_text": "The change is in and the acceptance test passes: all 4 scenarios in `bin/e2e`.\n\nThese totals are worked out in the front end, so the whole change is in `src/main/frontend/src/app/features/people/people.ts`. I didn't need to touch the server or the database.\n\n**Sheet totals now trimmed.** The sheet's settled total (`rollup-settled-total`), open total (`rollup-open-total`) and cut total (`rollup-cut-total`) now use the same trim rule as the due and overdue totals. When three or more people have a figure, the single highest and single lowest are left out. For the cut total, a person who isn't in any pool counts as 0.00, so everyone has a figure. The spec's numbers only work out that way.\n\n**New consolidated figures.** There are three new figures over the sheet and all the sheets below it: `consolidated-settled-total`, `consolidated-open-total` and `consolidated-cut-total`. Each is trimmed once over everyone in that tree, not sheet by sheet. For the cut total, the screen now also loads the pools of each sheet below, because cuts come from each sheet's own pools.\n\n**Two smaller points:**\n- I moved the code that adds up a person's cuts across pools into a shared helper, so the sheet's pools and the pools of the sheets below are handled the same way.\n- No audit records changed. The spec doesn't expect any for these totals.",
